      <Comment source="xue, PMN, nilo-poyanco, SRI, caspi">UDP-glucose is an activated form of glucose that participates in a variety of enzymatic reactions, including: 1. Biosynthesis of glucose-containing compounds, such as polysaccharaides (glycogen, starch, laminarin and cellulose), disaccharides (sucrose, trehalose), &amp;beta;-glucosides, and glucosyl-ceramides. 2. Channeling galactose into the glycolytic pathway It has also been suggested that UDP-D-glucose can act as an extracellular signaling molecule |CITS: [12695547]|.</Comment>
